title: Metarecord
tags: [[Data model]]
kind: overview
summary: A uuid, a version, and a multi-map of fields: the metadata about one subject — a file, a tag, a collection.

A metarecord is a coherent set of metadata about one subject — typically a file —
or a value such metadata shares (a tag, a collection, a duplicate group). Its
fields are its metadata: "metarecord" names the unit, "metadata" what its fields
say.

|!Part |!What |
|`uuid` |its stable identifier, 32 lowercase hex characters on the wire |
|`version` |a hash of its content, computed by the daemon ([[Metarecord version]]) |
|`fields` |its fields, each with the id of its row ([[Fields and values]]) |

```
{ "uuid": "3f2a…", "version": 8123456789,
  "fields": [ {"id": 42, "name": "rating", "value": {"type": "int", "value": 5}} ] }
```

A metarecord belongs to the repository whose store holds it: there is no owner
field, and a second owner cannot be expressed. Links between metarecords of two
repositories live outside the data model, in the sync state of that pair.

The zero uuid (`00000000000000000000000000000000`) is never a metarecord's: it
stands for "no parent" in a forest's root positions. A uuid is random (v4, 122
random bits): a collision among a billion metarecords has a probability of about
10⁻¹⁹.
